WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.040
Thanks for tuning in to Tesla Short's Time Daily episode 444. I'm Patrick in Vancouver.

00:00:05.260 --> 00:00:09.200
Today is April 22nd, 2026. There's a lot to cover in Tesla land today.

00:00:09.620 --> 00:00:12.400
Here's what's making news in the Tesla Short's time world today.

00:00:13.060 --> 00:00:17.680
The European market delivered some encouraging news for electric vehicles with sales across

00:00:17.680 --> 00:00:23.200
the region, up 11% in March. Tesla, along with several Chinese brands, helped drive much of

00:00:23.200 --> 00:00:28.120
that growth. It is a clear sign that in parts of Europe, the electric vehicle transition still has

00:00:28.120 --> 00:00:33.300
real momentum. At the same time, this growth is not uniform and depends heavily on local incentives

00:00:33.300 --> 00:00:38.380
and fuel prices. From a business perspective, these regional differences matter because they

00:00:38.380 --> 00:00:44.500
affect how Tesla allocates production and tailors its offerings. The fact that both Tesla and the

00:00:44.500 --> 00:00:49.680
Chinese makers led the way suggests customers are responding to value price and technology rather

00:00:49.680 --> 00:00:55.360
than brand loyalty alone. That patchwork reality is exactly why the conversation about who Tesla

00:00:55.360 --> 00:01:01.260
is actually competing against is changing. Ford's CEO was quite blunt in his assessment of the

00:01:01.260 --> 00:01:06.120
current landscape. He noted that Tesla has not delivered enough fresh product updates recently.

00:01:06.500 --> 00:01:11.520
More notably, he pointed to BYD as the competitor that deserves the closest attention instead of

00:01:11.520 --> 00:01:16.860
traditional automakers. This reflects a broader shift in the industry toward highly efficient Chinese

00:01:16.860 --> 00:01:22.460
manufacturers who are moving quickly on cost and scale. The competitive landscape is no longer just

00:01:22.460 --> 00:01:26.820
about legacy car companies with their large dealer networks and brand recognition.

00:01:27.400 --> 00:01:32.100
It is increasingly about who can deliver compelling vehicles at aggressive price points while

00:01:32.100 --> 00:01:37.760
improving technology at a rapid pace. For Tesla, this means the pressure is real, but it also

00:01:37.760 --> 00:01:43.820
clarifies where the real battle is being fought. While the pressure from China grows, Tesla is

00:01:43.820 --> 00:01:49.960
quietly locking in more of the hardware it needs on the AI side. Samsung is reportedly tripling its

00:01:49.960 --> 00:01:54.980
tram supply to Tesla according to recent reports. The increased demand comes from both the

00:01:54.980 --> 00:02:00.540
infotainment and computing systems inside the vehicles and the expanding AI training clusters.

00:02:01.120 --> 00:02:05.520
This move represents a significant scaling of the underlying hardware foundation.

00:02:06.000 --> 00:02:11.120
From a technology and supply chain perspective, it is a quiet indicator that Tesla continues to

00:02:11.120 --> 00:02:17.000
invest heavily in the infrastructure for its AI ambitions. Securing this level of memory supply now

00:02:17.000 --> 00:02:22.820
suggests confidence in future compute requirements across the board. It also highlights how the AI

00:02:22.820 --> 00:02:28.600
side of the business is becoming a major driver of component demand. That heavier compute demand is

00:02:28.600 --> 00:02:33.700
showing up in the car too with a new voice model rolling out. Tesla has started deploying a new voice

00:02:33.700 --> 00:02:39.240
model across its fleet of vehicles. The aim is to create a more natural sounding in-car assistant that

00:02:39.240 --> 00:02:46.980
feels less robotic in daily use. Owners often notice software improvements like this more than

00:02:46.980 --> 00:02:52.300
with the voice system on every drive. From a product experience standpoint, these updates can

00:02:52.300 --> 00:02:58.160
meaningfully improve satisfaction without requiring any hardware changes. It is the kind of iterative

00:02:58.160 --> 00:03:04.500
progress that keeps the existing fleet feeling current and cared for. Tesla has always leaned on over

00:03:04.500 --> 00:03:09.060
the air updates to evolve the ownership experience and this appears to be the latest example.

00:03:09.940 --> 00:03:14.820
Staying on the product side, there is a fresh look at the model Y variant that is carrying a lot of

00:03:15.020 --> 00:03:21.220
volume. A new analysis breaks down five key highlights of the model YL Premium. This version seems

00:03:21.220 --> 00:03:26.580
tailored for specific markets with particular attention to range build quality and the features that

00:03:26.580 --> 00:03:32.740
have made the model Y such a strong global seller. It is encouraging to see Tesla continue

00:03:32.740 --> 00:03:38.700
refining its highest volume vehicle rather than standing still. The focus on these attributes

00:03:38.700 --> 00:03:43.680
suggests the company is listening to what different regional customers actually value most.

00:03:43.680 --> 00:03:48.800
In a competitive market where buyers have more choices, every small improvement in the model Y

00:03:48.800 --> 00:03:55.120
helps maintain its position. Not all the product news is positive though and there is new NHTSA

00:03:55.120 --> 00:04:00.680
complaint data worth putting in context. The Model S currently leads in complaints per 10,000

00:04:00.680 --> 00:04:06.080
vehicles according to the latest figures. That number understandably raises eyebrows for owners

00:04:06.080 --> 00:04:11.400
and prospective buyers alike. Yet it is important to note that most of the top 10 vehicles on the list

00:04:11.400 --> 00:04:17.000
are still traditional gas powered models. The data does not erase legitimate frustrations some owners

00:04:17.000 --> 00:04:22.880
are experiencing, but it does sit inside a broader industry picture. Tesla has always encouraged

00:04:22.880 --> 00:04:28.420
transparent reporting and this is part of that reality. As the company pushes the boundaries of both

00:04:28.420 --> 00:04:34.300
performance and software, the complaint profile can look different from conventional cars. Let's step

00:04:34.300 --> 00:04:39.460
back from the weekly headlines for two evergreen segments that explain bigger pictures a lot of new

00:04:39.460 --> 00:04:45.300
listeners ask about. Battery chemistry has evolved considerably over the past decade and different

00:04:45.300 --> 00:04:50.780
regions are placing very different bets on what matters most. Early lithium ion cells relied heavily

00:04:50.780 --> 00:04:56.520
on cobalt, which created cost and ethical challenges around mining. The industry then moved toward

00:04:56.520 --> 00:05:03.140
NMC chemistries with varying nickel manganese and cobalt ratios to boost energy density and range.

00:05:03.600 --> 00:05:09.060
Tesla used these in many early Model 3 and Model Y vehicles, especially where highway range was a

00:05:09.060 --> 00:05:15.940
top priority. In China, the focus shifted strongly to LFP lithium iron phosphate because it is cheaper,

00:05:16.120 --> 00:05:21.640
more stable and offers excellent longevity with thousands of cycles. That approach allowed aggressive

00:05:21.640 --> 00:05:27.760
pricing and reduced dependence on scarce metals, even if the energy density is lower. Europe finds

00:05:27.760 --> 00:05:32.400
itself in the middle balancing strict efficiency rules with growing concerns about supply chain

00:05:32.400 --> 00:05:38.040
resilience. Some brands stick with high nickel cells for performance image while others adopt LFP to

00:05:38.040 --> 00:05:44.900
hit price targets. Tesla's own 4680 cells represent another bet by going tabless and larger in diameter

00:05:44.900 --> 00:05:49.860
to cut manufacturing costs and improve thermal performance. The structural pack enabled by these

00:05:49.860 --> 00:05:55.660
cells also reduces weight and complexity, which improves overall vehicle efficiency. What stands out

00:05:55.660 --> 00:06:00.520
is how the definition of good enough varies by market. North America often chases the biggest range

00:06:00.520 --> 00:06:06.560
number while China emphasizes cost per kilometer over the full life of the vehicle. Tesla's vertical

00:06:06.560 --> 00:06:10.880
integration gives it the flexibility to use different chemistries and different factories which is

00:06:10.880 --> 00:06:16.860
becoming a genuine strategic advantage. After batteries, the question I get most often is how does

00:06:16.860 --> 00:06:22.920
full-self driving actually work under the hood? The hardware journey began with autopilot hardware 2,

00:06:23.180 --> 00:06:30.820
then moved to HW3 with custom neural network chips. HW4 added more cameras and greater processing power

00:06:30.820 --> 00:06:38.340
and HW5 is on the horizon. The bold philosophical change came when Tesla went vision-only removing radar

00:06:38.340 --> 00:06:44.520
and relying on eight cameras because humans drive primarily with their eyes. Inside the system,

00:06:44.740 --> 00:06:49.880
an occupancy network builds a real-time three-dimensional understanding of the world around the car,

00:06:50.280 --> 00:06:56.280
rather than simple flat-bounding boxes. The planning layer now uses transformer models that

00:06:56.280 --> 00:07:02.000
learn from millions of miles of real-world data instead of hand-coded rules. This contrasts with

00:07:02.000 --> 00:07:07.300
companies like Waymo that use multiple sensor types and operate in geofenced mapped areas with backup

00:07:07.300 --> 00:07:13.280
operators. Tesla's approach is to improve everywhere at once because every customer vehicle collects data

00:07:13.280 --> 00:07:19.860
with no geographic limits. The bet is that massive real-world data plus neural networks will ultimately

00:07:19.860 --> 00:07:25.820
scale better and more affordably than adding complexity at the hardware level. There is still work

00:07:25.820 --> 00:07:30.900
ahead on regulatory approval and edge cases, but the architecture is built on copying the most

00:07:30.900 --> 00:07:36.920
successful driver on the planet, which is collective human experience. It is an engineering philosophy that

00:07:36.920 --> 00:07:42.220
explains why Tesla talks so much about its data advantage. These two deep topics batteries and

00:07:42.220 --> 00:07:48.040
full-self driving really are the long-term bets that matter. While weekly sales numbers and competitive

00:07:48.040 --> 00:07:54.060
noise will continue to fluctuate the progress and chemistry flexibility and in the vision-based AI

00:07:54.060 --> 00:07:59.840
architecture will shape what Tesla becomes over the next decade. Before we go keep an eye on how the

00:07:59.840 --> 00:08:03.960
new voice model performs in owner feedback and any further signals on AI hardware scaling.

